  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN such that:\n\n\n2×(A1⊕A2⊕…⊕AN)≥(A1∣A2∣…∣AN)2\\times (A_1 \\oplus A_2 \\oplus \\ldots \\oplus A_N) \\geq (A_1 | A_2 | \\ldots | A_N)2×(A1​⊕A2​⊕…⊕AN​)≥(A1​∣A2​∣…∣AN​), where ⊕\\oplus⊕ and ∣|∣ denote the bitwise xor and or operations respectively.\nYour task is to perform the following operation until the array is empty:\n\n\nChoose any element AiA_iAi​ from the array.\nRemove AiA_iAi​ from the array.\nPerform **one** of the following:\n\nUse a new box and add AiA_iAi​ to the box.\nSelect an existing box such that the XOR of all the elements in the box (before placing AiA_iAi​) is **greater than or equal to** AiA_iAi​ and add AiA_iAi​ to the box.\n\n\nDetermine the **minimum** number of boxes required to empty the array AAA.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN — the number of elements in AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1,A_2,\\ldots,A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, the elements of the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the **minimum** number of boxes required to empty the array AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤10181 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^{18}1≤Ai​≤1018",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1\n6\n4\n1 2 3 12\n3\n6 5 4",
        "output": "1\n1\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\nChoose 666 from the array and delete it.\n\nAdd 666 to a new box.\n\n\n\nAAA is empty now and we used one box.\nTest case 222:\n\nChoose 121212 from the array and delete it.\n\nAdd 121212 to a new box. The XOR of the box becomes 121212.\n\n\nChoose 333 from the array and delete it.\n\nSince the XOR of the box 12≥312 \\geq 312≥3, we can add 333 to the box. The XOR of the box becomes 12⊕3=1512\\oplus3=1512⊕3=15.\n\n\nChoose 222 from the array and delete it.\n\nSince the XOR of the box 15≥215 \\geq 215≥2, we can add 222 to the box. The XOR of the box becomes 15⊕2=1315\\oplus2=1315⊕2=13.\n\n\nChoose 111 from the array and delete it.\n\nSince the XOR of the box 13≥113 \\geq 113≥1, we can add 111 to the box. The XOR of the box becomes 13⊕1=1213\\oplus1=1213⊕1=12.\n\n\n\nAAA is empty now and we used one box.\nTest case 333:\n\nChoose 555 from the array and delete it.\n\nAdd 555 to a new box. The XOR of the box becomes 555.\n\n\nChoose 444 from the array and delete it.\n\nSince the XOR of the box 5≥45 \\geq 45≥4, we can add 444 to the box. The XOR of the box becomes 5⊕4=15\\oplus4=15⊕4=1.\n\n\nChoose 666 from the array and delete it.\n\nAdd 666 to a new box. The XOR of the second box is 666.\n\n\n\nAAA is now empty and we used two boxes."
      }
    ]
  },
